   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th head and neck mucosal melanoma & AJCC 8th staging",
    "intro": "Primary mucosal melanoma of the head and neck begins at pT3 (mucosa/submucosa); pT4a involves deep soft tissue, muscle, cartilage, bone or overlying skin; pT4b involves brain, dura, skull base, lower cranial nerves (IX–XII), masticator space, carotid artery, prevertebral space or mediastinum.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Morphology, immunohistochemistry & molecular testing",
      "points": [
       "Pleomorphic epithelioid, spindled, plasmacytoid or small round cell sheets with prominent cherry-red nucleoli, intranuclear pseudoinclusions, necrosis and variable (or absent) melanin pigment.",
       "Confirm melanocytic lineage with SOX10, S100, Melan-A, HMB45 and/or PRAME (amelanotic tumours mimic SNUC, lymphoma, olfactory neuroblastoma or sarcoma).",
       "Molecular profile differs from cutaneous melanoma: KIT, NRAS and SF3B1 mutations are enriched while BRAF V600E is uncommon."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Sinonasal and Oral Mucosal Melanoma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
